{"id":"mahabharata-7-076","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":76,"title":"षट्सप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 76 · Arjuna and Krishna advance again","summary":{"en":"The Kauravas tremble at the sight of Arjuna and Krishna, who go on toward Jayadratha talking of the day's task. All beings think that the two are more than Drona's army can stop.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ-ಕೃಷ್ಣರನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಕೌರವರು ನಡುಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವರು ದಿನದ ಕಾರ್ಯದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಮಾತನಾಡುತ್ತಾ ಜಯದ್ರಥನತ್ತ ಸಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ದ್ರೋಣನ ಸೈನ್ಯವೂ ಅವರನ್ನು ತಡೆಯಲಾರದೆಂದು ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಭಾವಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन और कृष्ण को देखकर कौरव काँपते हैं, और वे दिन के कार्य की चर्चा करते हुए जयद्रथ की ओर बढ़ते हैं। सभी प्राणी मानते हैं कि द्रोण की सेना भी उन्हें रोक नहीं सकती।","te":"అర్జున కృష్ణులను చూసి కౌరవులు వణుకుతారు; వారు ఆ రోజు కార్యం గురించి మాట్లాడుతూ జయద్రథుని వైపు సాగుతారు. ద్రోణుని సేన కూడా వారిని ఆపలేదని అందరూ భావిస్తారు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனனையும் கண்ணனையும் கண்டு கௌரவர் நடுங்குகின்றனர்; அவர்கள் அன்றைய பணியைப் பேசியபடி ஜயத்ரதனை நோக்கிச் செல்கின்றனர். த்ரோணரின் படையாலும் அவர்களைத் தடுக்க முடியாது என்று எல்லா உயிர்களும் எண்ணுகின்றன.","ml":"അർജുനനെയും കൃഷ്ണനെയും കണ്ട് കൗരവർ വിറയ്ക്കുന്നു; ദിവസത്തെ ദൗത്യത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് സംസാരിച്ച് അവർ ജയദ്രഥന്റെ നേർക്ക് തുടർന്നു പോകുന്നു. ദ്രോണരുടെ സേനയ്ക്ക് തടയാനാവാത്തവിധം ഇരുവരും അധികമാണെന്ന് എല്ലാ ജീവികളും കരുതുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.76; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स्रंसन्त इव मज्जानस्तावकानां भयान्नृप ।\nतौ दृष्ट्वा समतिक्रान्तौ वासुदेवधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vasudeva and Dhananjaya pass on, the very marrow of your men seemed to melt with fear, O king."}},{"n":2,"text":"सर्वे तु प्रतिसंरब्धा ह्रीमन्तः सत्त्वचोदिताः ।\nस्थिरीबूता महात्मानः प्रत्यगच्छन्धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But all those who were modest and moved by courage grew furious, steadied themselves, and, great-souled, went back against Dhananjaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"ये गताः पाण्डवं युद्धे क्रोधामर्षसमन्विताः ।\nतेऽद्यापि न निवर्तन्ते सिन्धवः सागरादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who went against the Pandava in battle full of anger and impatience do not return even now, like rivers from the sea."}},{"n":4,"text":"असन्तस्तु न्यवर्तन्त वेदेभ्य इव नास्तिकाः ।\nनरकं भजमानास्ते प्रत्यपद्यन्त किल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the ignoble turned back, like unbelievers from the Vedas, heading for hell, and so took on guilt."}},{"n":5,"text":"तावतीत्य रथानीकं विमुक्तौ पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nददृशाते यथा राहोरास्यान्मुक्तौ प्रभाकरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing beyond the chariot division, the two best of men, set free, looked like two suns released from the mouth of Rahu."}},{"n":6,"text":"मत्स्याविव महाजालं विदार्य विगतज्वरौ ।\nतथा कृष्णावदृश्येतां सेनाजालं विदार्य तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As two fish free of fever tear a great net, so the two Krishnas were seen, having torn that net of an army."}},{"n":7,"text":"विमुक्तौ शस्त्रसंबाधाद्द्रोणानीकात्सुदुर्भिदात् ।\nअदृश्येतां महात्मानौ कालसूर्याविवोदितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from the press of weapons, from Drona's hard-to-break division, the two great-souled ones were seen like two suns of the end of time risen."}},{"n":8,"text":"अस्त्रसंबाधनिर्मुक्तौ विमुक्तौ शस्त्रसंकटात् ।\nअदृश्येतां महात्मानौ शत्रुसंबाधकारिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Released from the crush of missiles and the strait of weapons, those two great-souled ones, who crushed their enemies, were seen."}},{"n":9,"text":"विमुक्तौ ज्वलनस्पर्शान्मकरास्याज्झषाविव ।\nव्यक्षोभयेतां सेनां तौ समुद्रं मकराविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from the touch of fire, like two fish from a sea-monster's mouth, those two stirred up the army as two sea-monsters stir the ocean."}},{"n":10,"text":"तावकास्तव पुत्राश्च द्रोणानीकस्थयोस्तयोः ।\nनैतौ तरिष्यतो द्रोणमिति चक्रुस्तदा मतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your men and your sons, seeing the two in the midst of Drona's army, then decided: These two will not cross Drona."}},{"n":11,"text":"तौ तु दृष्ट्वा व्यतिक्रान्तौ द्रोणानीकं महाद्युती ।\nनाशशंसुर्महाराज सिन्धुराजस्य जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But seeing the two radiant ones pass beyond Drona's division, they no longer hoped for the life of the Sindhu king."}},{"n":12,"text":"आशा बलवती राजन्पुत्राणामभवत्तव ।\nद्रोणहार्दिक्ययोः कृष्णौ न मोक्ष्येते इति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great hope, O king, had been in your sons: that the two Krishnas would not escape Drona and the son of Hridika."}},{"n":13,"text":"तामाशां विफलां कृत्वा निस्तीर्णौ तौ परंतपौ ।\nद्रोणानीकं महाराज भोजानीकं च दुस्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made that hope fruitless, those two scorchers of foes crossed Drona's division and the hard-to-cross division of the Bhojas."}},{"n":14,"text":"अथ दृष्ट्वा व्यतिक्रान्तौ ज्वलिताविव पावकौ ।\nनिराशाः सिन्धुराजस्य जीवितं नाशशंसिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them pass, like two blazing fires, they gave up hope for the life of the king of the Sindhus."}},{"n":15,"text":"मिथश्च समभाषेतामभीतौ भयवर्धनौ ।\nजयद्रथवधे वाचस्तास्ताः कृष्णधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two, fearless and fear-spreading, Krishna and Dhananjaya, spoke to each other many such words about killing Jayadratha."}},{"n":16,"text":"असौ मध्ये कृतः षड्भिर्धार्तराष्ट्रैर्महारथैः ।\nचक्षुर्विषयसंप्राप्तो न नौ मोक्ष्यति सैन्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said: There he is, placed in the middle by six great chariot-warriors of Dhritarashtra's side; now that he is within sight, the Saindhava will not escape us."}},{"n":17,"text":"यद्यस्य समरे गोप्ता शक्रो देवगणैः सह ।\nतथाप्येनं हनिष्याव इति कृष्णावभाषताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if Shakra with the hosts of gods were his protector in the battle, we would still kill him. So the two Krishnas said."}},{"n":18,"text":"इति कृष्णौ महाबाहू मिथः कथयतां तदा ।\nसिन्धुराजमवेक्षन्तौ तत्पुत्रास्तव शुश्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons heard the mighty-armed Krishnas speaking thus to each other, as they looked at the king of the Sindhus."}},{"n":19,"text":"अतीत्य मरुधन्वेव प्रयान्तौ तृषितौ गजौ ।\nपीत्वा वारि समाश्वस्तौ तथैवास्तामरिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two thirsty elephants crossing a desert and going on, refreshed after drinking water, so those two subduers of foes stood."}},{"n":20,"text":"व्याघ्रसिंहगजाकीर्णानतिक्रम्येव पर्वतान् ।\nअदृश्येतां महाबाहू यथा मृत्युजरातिगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two who had passed over mountains thick with tigers, lions and elephants, those mighty-armed ones were seen as if beyond death and old age."}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा हि मुखवर्णोऽयमनयोरिति मेनिरे ।\nतावका दृश्य मुक्तौ तौ विक्रोशन्ति स्म सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So they thought, for such was the colour of their faces. Seeing them freed, your men cried out on all sides."}},{"n":22,"text":"द्रोणादाशीविषाकाराज्ज्वलितादिव पावकात् ।\nअन्येभ्यः पार्थिवेभ्यश्च भास्वन्ताविव भास्करौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from Drona, who was like a venomous snake or blazing fire, and from other kings, they shone like two suns."}},{"n":23,"text":"तौ मुक्तौ सागरप्रख्याद्द्रोणानीकादरिंदमौ ।\nअदृश्येतां मुदा युक्तौ समुत्तीर्यार्णवं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from Drona's division, which was like the sea, those two subduers of foes were seen full of joy, like men who have crossed the ocean."}},{"n":24,"text":"शस्त्रौघान्महतो मुक्तौ द्रोणहार्दिक्यरक्षितान् ।\nरोचमानावदृश्येतामिन्द्राग्न्योः सदृशौ रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from the great floods of weapons guarded by Drona and Hridika's son, they shone in the battle like Indra and Agni."}},{"n":25,"text":"उद्भिन्नरुधिरौ कृष्णौ भारद्वाजस्य सायकैः ।\nशितैश्चितौ व्यरोचेतां कर्णिकारैरिवाचलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their blood welling from the arrows of Bharadvaja's son, the two Krishnas, studded with the sharp shafts, shone like two mountains covered with karnikara blossoms."}},{"n":26,"text":"द्रोणग्राहह्रदान्मुक्तौ शक्त्याशीविषसंकटात् ।\nअयःशरोग्रमकरात्क्षत्रियप्रवराम्भसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were freed from the pool of Drona's crocodile, the straits of spears and venomous serpents, the fierce sea-monsters of iron arrows, the waters of the best kshatriyas,"}},{"n":27,"text":"ज्याघोषतलनिर्ह्रादाद्गदानिस्त्रिंशविद्युतः ।\nद्रोणास्त्रमेघान्निर्मुक्तौ सूर्येन्दू तिमिरादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"the roar of bowstrings and palms, the lightning of maces and swords, the clouds of Drona's weapons, like the sun and the moon freed from darkness."}},{"n":28,"text":"बाहुभ्यामिव संतीर्णौ सिन्धुषष्ठाः समुद्रगाः ।\nतपान्ते सरितः पूर्णा महाग्राहसमाकुलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They had crossed, as it were, with their arms, like rivers going to the sea, full at the end of the heat, thick with great crocodiles, the Sindhu as sixth."}},{"n":29,"text":"इति कृष्णौ महेष्वासौ यशसा लोकविश्रुतौ ।\nसर्वभूतान्यमन्यन्त द्रोणास्त्रबलविस्मयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So all beings thought of those two great archers, famous in the world for their glory, in amazement at the might of Drona's weapons."}},{"n":30,"text":"जयद्रथं समीपस्थमवेक्षन्तौ जिघांसया ।\nरुरुं निपाने लिप्सन्तौ व्याघ्रवत्तावतिष्ठताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking at Jayadratha near them, wishing to kill him, they stood like two tigers who long for a deer at the water-place."}},{"n":31,"text":"यथा हि मुखवर्णोऽयमनयोरिति मेनिरे ।\nतव योधा महाराज हतमेव जयद्रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your warriors, great king, for the same reason, the colour of their faces, thought Jayadratha already slain."}},{"n":32,"text":"लोहिताक्षौ महाबाहू संयत्तौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nसिन्धुराजमभिप्रेक्ष्य हृष्टौ व्यनदतां मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed Krishna and Pandava, red-eyed and alert, seeing the king of the Sindhus, shouted again and again with joy."}},{"n":33,"text":"शौरेरभीशुहस्तस्य पार्थस्य च धनुष्मतः ।\nतयोरासीत्प्रतिभ्राजः सूर्यपावकयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brightness of Shauri, rein in hand, and of Partha with his bow, was like that of the sun and fire together."}},{"n":34,"text":"हर्ष एव तयोरासीद्द्रोणानीकप्रमुक्तयोः ।\nसमीपे सैन्धवं दृष्ट्वा श्येनयोरामिषं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their joy, freed from Drona's division, was like that of two hawks seeing meat near, at the sight of the Saindhava close by."}},{"n":35,"text":"तौ तु सैन्धवमालोक्य वर्तमानमिवान्तिके ।\nसहसा पेततुः क्रुद्धौ क्षिप्रं श्येनाविवामिषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Saindhava as if near at hand, the two, angry, swiftly fell on him like two hawks on meat."}},{"n":36,"text":"तौ तु दृष्ट्वा व्यतिक्रान्तौ हृषीकेशधनंजयौ ।\nसिन्धुराजस्य रक्षार्थं पराक्रान्तः सुतस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the two, Hrishikesha and Dhananjaya, pass on, your valiant son Duryodhana came forward to protect the king of the Sindhus."}},{"n":37,"text":"द्रोणेनाबद्धकवचो राजा दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nययावेकरथेनाजौ हयसंस्कारवित्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Duryodhana, with armour bound on by Drona, went in a single chariot into the battle, lord, being skilled in the care of horses."}},{"n":38,"text":"कृष्णपार्थौ महेष्वासौ व्यतिक्रम्याथ ते सुतः ।\nअग्रतः पुण्डरीकाक्षं प्रतीयाय नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing the two great archers Krishna and Partha, your son, O king, came back to face the lotus-eyed Krishna from in front."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततः सर्वेषु सैन्येषु वादित्राणि प्रहृष्टवत् ।\nप्रावाद्यन्समतिक्रान्ते तव पुत्रे धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in all the armies instruments were played joyfully when your son had gone past Dhananjaya."}},{"n":40,"text":"सिंहनादरवाश्चासञ्शङ्खदुन्दुभिमिश्रिताः ।\nदृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनं तत्र कृष्णयोः प्रमुखे स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lion-roars arose, mixed with conches and drums, when they saw Duryodhana standing before the two Krishnas."}},{"n":41,"text":"ये च ते सिन्धुराजस्य गोप्तारः पावकोपमाः ।\nते प्रहृष्यन्त समरे दृष्ट्वा पुत्रं तवाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those protectors of the king of the Sindhus, who were like fire, rejoiced in the battle, seeing your son, my lord."}},{"n":42,"text":"दृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनं कृष्णस्त्वतिक्रान्तं सहानुगम् ।\nअब्रवीदर्जुनं राजन्प्राप्तकालमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Duryodhana come on, with his followers, Krishna said to Arjuna these words, O king, now that the time had come."}}]}]}